{"type":"standard","title":"Ahlon language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ahlon language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35412","titles":{"canonical":"Ahlon_language","normalized":"Ahlon language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ahlon language</span></span>"},"pageid":33181547,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1325425405","tid":"0bbdd1ce-cfe3-11f0-8bb8-af6a0b4d8bb2","timestamp":"2025-12-03T00:57:31Z","description":"Kwa language spoken in Togo","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahlon_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahlon_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahlon_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ahlon_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahlon_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ahlon_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahlon_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ahlon_language"}},"extract":"The Ahlon language, Igo, is spoken in the Plateau Region of Togo. It is considered one of the Ghana–Togo Mountain languages of the Kwa family. Variations of its official name are Achlo, Ahlõ, Ahlo, Ahlon-Bogo, Ahonlan, Anlo.","extract_html":"<p>The <b>Ahlon</b> language, <i><b>Igo</b></i>, is spoken in the Plateau Region of Togo. It is considered one of the Ghana–Togo Mountain languages of the Kwa family. Variations of its official name are <i>Achlo, Ahlõ, Ahlo, Ahlon-Bogo, Ahonlan, Anlo</i>.</p>"}